  @typescript-eslint/consistent-type-definitions  Use an `interface` instead of a `type` here. Both describe the same object shape, but an interface is the one this project writes: it can be reopened by a later declaration, it shows up under its own name in compiler errors rather than being expanded inline, and mixing the two spellings for the same job makes a reader ask whether the difference was meant.

